  timingType: "Chain (Features the highly refined EA888 Gen 4 timing chain system. Audi extensively reinforced the chain, guides, and hydraulic tensioner to ensure they outlast the vehicle's functional lifespan. Mechanical elongation is extremely rare, but standard VCDS phase adaptation monitoring at high mileage remains a good preventative measure to ensure optimal valve timing.)", injectionType: "Direct Injection (FSI. Built for strict Euro 6d-ISC-FCM emissions regulations, the EA888 Gen 4 utilizes an ultra-high-pressure 350-bar direct injection system alongside twin Gasoline Particulate Filters (GPF/OPF). Because the intake valves are not washed by fuel, periodic physical intake valve carbon cleaning via walnut blasting may eventually be required over 100,000 km.)", engineLifespan: "250,000+ km (The EA888 Gen 4 block is an absolute marvel of modern engineering. By entirely eliminating the oil consumption issues of Gen 2 and utilizing advanced lower-friction internals, the core engine will easily outlast the chassis. The primary threats are the electronic wastegate actuator, plastic water pump module, and potential GPF clogging if driven exclusively on short urban trips.)", turboType: "Turbocharged (Equipped with a highly optimized, fast-spooling Garrett/Continental turbocharger specific to the Gen 4 architecture. It delivers immediate low-end torque and excellent throttle response, though the electronic wastegate actuator is integrated and requires periodic calibration via VCDS if serviced.)", ecuType: "Continental SIMOS 19.x (An incredibly advanced, heavily encrypted engine management unit that controls the complex 350-bar fueling parameters necessary to keep the Gasoline Particulate Filter (GPF) clean while delivering 245hp. Tuning unlocks massive torque, but requires highly specialized mapping to safely accommodate the restrictive GPF backpressure.)", euroStandard: "Euro 6d-ISC-FCM (With OPF/GPF)", maxPowerStockInternals: "420 - 450 hp (The factory forged connecting rods, pistons, and crankshaft are remarkably stout. The engine block effortlessly handles massive boost increases. However, pushing past Stage 1 power levels generally requires the removal or replacement of the highly restrictive factory GPF system, which introduces legal and emissions complexities.)",
